# Runtime Isolation

Use the weakest runtime only when its isolation is sufficient for the lab threat model.

Conceptual classes:
- standard container for lower-risk web training,
- sandboxed container such as gVisor when meaningful code execution is expected,
- microVM/full VM such as Firecracker/KVM for stronger isolation, kernel/malware/AD/Windows scenarios.

Mandatory defaults:
- no privileged containers,
- no Docker socket mounts,
- no host PID/IPC/network modes,
- no sensitive host filesystem mounts,
- drop Linux capabilities by default,
- apply CPU, memory, PID, disk/IO and bandwidth limits,
- use seccomp/AppArmor/LSM controls where applicable.

Rootless mode is defense in depth, not the sole boundary. Runtime configuration must satisfy the Lab Manifest schema and Security Model.
